Credits, under About

Volkdude's credits is a page inside Settings, directly under About: the page that says whose
edition this is, followed by the page that says whose work it is built on. Eric Hartford's name
is the first section of it, because none of QuixiDesk exists without his work.

What it adds:

  resources/ui/credits.md        The document itself. Written as prose, not a settings form: one
                                 measure, one leading, a clear step between heading levels.

  resources/ui/app.js            creditsInline() and creditsSection(). The first formats **bold**
                                 and bare http(s) links, and nothing else. The second fetches the
                                 file and renders it, then a per-skill table from the manifest.
                                 Both sit directly above settingsPage().

  resources/ui/app.css           The measure, the leading, and the two-column per-skill rows.

The credit on `with`, the one bundled skill this edition ships, is set by scripts/sanitize-tree.py
rather than by this patch. That script decides which manifest entries survive, so it is the only
place that can credit them without being written against a manifest that no longer exists; a hunk
here would have to match the manifest mid-chain and would break the moment the filter changed.

  crates/quixi-engine/src/lib.rs The manifest reader passes `credit` through untouched. Without
                                 this the field reaches the manifest and stops there, and a skill
                                 card names a tool with no author.

Why the engine change is in the same patch as the interface: a page that renders a table of
authors who never arrive looks like a page that works. This was the bug -- the field was written,
mapped, and dropped.

The page is plain text plus the two formattings above. No markdown engine: an asterisk left on the
page makes a document look like a draft, and a link you cannot click in a credits page is a name
with no address.

