+# Volkdude's credits
+
+Every tool this build drives belongs to somebody else. This file says whose.
+
+## 1. Eric Hartford — QuixiDesk
+
+**Eric Hartford wrote QuixiDesk** (QuixiAI, MIT). The window, the workspace, the webview, the
+protocol, the bundled office skills — the whole thing this edition is an alteration of. Every line
+of this package sits on top of his work, and the first credit belongs to him, not to the person who
+altered it.
+
+He is the person behind QuixiAI (x.com/QuixiAI, erichartford.com), known for the Dolphin and Samantha
+models. QuixiDesk is his: https://github.com/QuixiAI/QuixiDesk
+
+### Why his harness and not mine
+
+He had been working on a harness of his own. It has more in it than this one does, but it lives in
+chaotic ADHD order, and a fool admires complexity while a genius admires simplicity. Eric's looked
+infinitely better. That is the honest reason this fork exists: the value in these tools is fairly
+simple, and the way he was presenting it could be simplified and made a great deal more elegant than
+it was.
+
+He also does not have nearly the experience a lot of people in this game have. In some areas he does.
+In many areas, no, not really — and he would rather write that down than let a credits page imply
+otherwise.
+
+### An open offer to Eric
+
+This edition is a fork, and it was made without asking. That is worth saying plainly rather than
+burying under a thank-you.
+
+**He would like to talk about any of it.** If a change here is wrong, ill-judged, or just irritates
+the piss out of you, say which one and he will discuss it — including reverting it. Nothing in this
+fork is more important to him than not making the original author's work worse, or making him feel
+that his own project was taken away from him.
+
+**He would genuinely like your approval, and knows that asking for it is not itself a humble act.**
+He asked for it to be written this way anyway, because the asking comes from a humble place: he is
+not asking to be endorsed, he is saying he would rather be told no than ship something you would
+object to. If the answer is that you would rather this fork did not exist, that is an answer he will
+take without argument.
+
